      "title": "Residual mass is not one more color",
      "html": "<figure class=\"volume6\" data-v6=\"V47\" id=\"visual-V47\" lang=\"en\"><header><span>V47</span><h3>Residual mass is not one more color</h3></header><p class=\"v6-intro\">Do points outside the positive mass bands share one residual class, or form separate singletons?</p><div class=\"v5-controls\" role=\"group\"><button type=\"button\" data-dust=\"0\" aria-pressed=\"false\">d=0</button><button type=\"button\" data-dust=\"25\" aria-pressed=\"true\">d=1/4</button><button type=\"button\" data-dust=\"50\" aria-pressed=\"false\">d=1/2</button></div><div class=\"v6-pair\"><section><h4>Map locations to classes</h4><img src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-volume6-v1/V47-en-25-0.svg\" alt=\"Map locations to classes\" data-pane=\"0\"></section><section><h4>Forget locations; keep classes</h4><img src=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-volume6-v1/V47-en-25-1.svg\" alt=\"Forget locations; keep classes\" data-pane=\"1\"></section></div><output data-result aria-live=\"polite\">Same-block probability = s1²+s2² = 0.3125; do not add d².</output><details><summary>Model assumptions and mathematical limits</summary><p>Deterministic paintbox masses s1=1/2, s2=1/2-d, with d=0,1/4,1/2; omit zero bands. Given masses, each individual samples an independent uniform point; shared positive bands define a class, while residual points are singletons. Six fixed positions illustrate the rule, not frequencies or their limiting theorem. Residual mass is not a shared color; d squared is not added to the same-block probability s1 squared+s2 squared. Random masses require Kingman mixing, common null sets and measurable ranking. A static paintbox does not specify coalescent clocks: pair rate 1 is an additional Kingman rule.</p></details><figcaption id=\"visual-V47-end\">The diagram explains a specific model in the text; full theorems and proofs remain in the chapter and its foundations.</figcaption><nav><a href=\"/assets/visuals/explanatory-volume6-v1/V47.en.svg\">SVG</a><a href=\"/print/V47.en.html\">Static print</a></nav></figure>",
      "condition": "Deterministic paintbox masses s1=1/2, s2=1/2-d, with d=0,1/4,1/2; omit zero bands. Given masses, each individual samples an independent uniform point; shared positive bands define a class, while residual points are singletons. Six fixed positions illustrate the rule, not frequencies or their limiting theorem. Residual mass is not a shared color; d squared is not added to the same-block probability s1 squared+s2 squared. Random masses require Kingman mixing, common null sets and measurable ranking. A static paintbox does not specify coalescent clocks: pair rate 1 is an additional Kingman rule.",
